    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = y+xy^{5}, \left(5,1\right), \left(-5,-5\right), \left(4,-2\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(5,1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-5,-5\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(4,-2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>15620</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-130</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(5,1\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(5,1) = 1  + 5(1)^{5} = 6</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-5,-5\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-5,-5) = -5   - 5(-5)^{5} = 15620</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(4,-2\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(4,-2) = -2  + 4(-2)^{5} = -130</m>.


</solution>
